    <!-- About Section -->
    <section id="about">
        <div class="container">
            <h2 class="section-title fade-in">About Me</h2>
            <p class="section-subtitle fade-in">Building Bridges Between Cloud & Innovation</p>

            <div class="about-content">
                <div class="about-text fade-in">
                    <p>
                        Hello! I'm <span class="highlight">Zechariah Kasina</span>, a Senior DevOps Engineer at
                        <span class="highlight">Amazon Web Services</span> based in Lake Oswego, Oregon.
                        I specialize in creating scalable cloud infrastructure, serverless applications,
                        and AI-powered solutions that solve real-world challenges.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        My mission is to bridge the gap between cutting-edge AWS services and practical
                        implementations that developers can learn from. Whether it's Infrastructure as Code
                        templates, AI document processors, or automation scripts, I'm passionate about
                        making complex cloud technologies accessible.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I spend my days working with <span class="highlight">ECS Fargate, Lambda, and Amazon Bedrock</span>,
                        while contributing educational content to the AWS Community. I'm particularly excited
                        about emerging technologies like Model Context Protocol servers and building practical
                        tools for document processing and content management.
                    </p>
